{"event": "workflow_authored", "run_id": "6cb6308939b44522b7f5df02646f024c", "pid": 216250, "time": "2026-10-11T10:59:06-0700", "elapsed_s": 0.017, "nodes": 33, "size_kb": 78, "static_errors": [], "notes": "Unresolved points and assumptions (from the documents): (1) Silence: decided 7/9 Oct = two short repeats, third silence 'Sesinizi alamad\u0131\u011f\u0131m i\u00e7in g\u00f6r\u00fc\u015fmeyi sonland\u0131r\u0131yorum.' and hang up; silence timing never sent by the bank, so this relies on a global intent node plus the platform inactivity monitor. (2) Wait time before a slow service counts as failed is still open (Mert/Deniz); engine calls use 20 s timeouts. The 'Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.' filler is not spoken because the first sentence must already carry data. (3) No service says whether the statement-week right is already used (pre-check pending with Mert/Kerem), so the change is always offered; after a change in this call it is not offered again. The limit is once per calendar year (Kerem, 7 Oct), which replaces the IVR 'ayda bir / y\u0131lda \u00fc\u00e7' prompts. A refusal from statement.week.change goes to the agent with the statement-week error sentence. (4) Amounts are written as digits with Turkish separators plus full currency names, and kuru\u015f/sent/peni are spoken as units. TTS speaks the digits. Last four digits are given digit by digit. (5) statement.pdf.send currencyType for multi-currency cards is not specified; 'TL' is sent. (6) No wording was given for the remaining automatic payment; a neutral sentence is used only when the flag is Y, the amount is >0 and the due date has passed. (7) No-debt reading: the due date is lastPayDate if not passed, else nextLastPayDate. In this branch there is no e-mail/week offer (Deniz's proposal was not agreed). Foreign-currency future totals are not read (open with Kerem). (8) The transferAmount line (analysis 4.4) was never drafted, so it is not spoken. (9) The 'change it?' question and the week options are merged into one question. (10) Bearer token not provided, so the Authorization header is omitted (test environment does not check it). (11) Third-party callers get the security sentence and the call ends toward the IVR login step; no transfer code is defined (Q8 follow"}
